-- title:
--   Kernel of a reduction map equals an extended prime
-- statement:
--   Let $P_0$ and $B$ be commutative rings with $B$ a $P_0$-algebra that is integral over $P_0$ and satisfies the going-down property, let $\kappa$ be a field and $\pi : B \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism, and let $\mathfrak{p}_0$ be a prime ideal of $P_0$. Assume: (i) the contraction of $\ker \pi$ along $P_0 \to B$ is exactly $\mathfrak{p}_0$; (ii) there is a subring $R \subseteq B$ containing the image of every element of $P_0$, such that (ii-a) every $b \in B$ admits $r, s \in R$ with $\pi(s) \neq 0$ and $b s = r$, and (ii-b) every $r \in R$ with $\pi(r) = 0$ can be written $r = \iota(c) r'$ with $c \in \mathfrak{p}_0$, $r' \in R$, where $\iota$ denotes the structure map $P_0 \to B$; (iii) the extended ideal $\mathfrak{p}_0 B = \mathrm{Ideal.map}\,\iota\,\mathfrak{p}_0$ is radical in the weak sense that $b^n \in \mathfrak{p}_0 B$ for some $n > 0$ implies $b \in \mathfrak{p}_0 B$. Then $\ker \pi = \mathfrak{p}_0 B$.
--
--   A commutative-algebra criterion identifying the kernel of a reduction map to a field with the ideal generated by the image of a prime of the base, under an integrality-plus-going-down hypothesis together with a denominator-and-divisibility condition supplied by an auxiliary subring. It is used in the characteristic-$p$ models of modular curves, where it yields the statements [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_eq_const_mul_of_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_eq_const_mul_of_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero) and its companion, extracting from the vanishing of a reduction map a factorisation by a constant from $\mathfrak{p}_0$.
